FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-distance-field.
OFF THE RECORD: March rays through two spheres and a floor. The distance
OFF THE RECORD: field returns the nearest signed distance to their surfaces.
OFF THE RECORD: Estimate normals from neighboring distances and cast a
OFF THE RECORD: second ray toward the light for a hard shadow.
OFF THE RECORD: All world coordinates use 1000 integer units per one.

HEREINAFTER, hit-epsilon SHALL MEAN 4.
HEREINAFTER, far-limit SHALL MEAN 9000.
HEREINAFTER, march-limit SHALL MEAN 48.
THE EXHIBIT OF march-result, COMPRISING hit AND x AND y AND z AND steps.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT wide IS 20.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tall IS 10.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ramp IS " .:-=+*#%@".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS "".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS 0.
ARTICLE 2.
    OFF THE RECORD: One row spans twice the angle of one column, to account
    OFF THE RECORD: for terminal cells that are about twice as tall as wide.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT vy IS ((tall LESS 1) LESS 2 TIMES row) TIMES 3000 APPORTIONED AMONG (wide LESS 1) LESS 400.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS 0.
ARTICLE 3.
    OFF THE RECORD: Normalize each perspective ray. Its length is never zero
    OFF THE RECORD: because its z component is 1800 before normalization.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT vx IS (2 TIMES column LESS (wide LESS 1)) TIMES 1500 APPORTIONED AMONG (wide LESS 1).
    OFF THE RECORD: Add one to the floor root so normalization never creates
    OFF THE RECORD: a vector longer than one world unit through rounding.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT vlength IS (THE FINDING OF field-root REGARDING vx TIMES vx PLUS vy TIMES vy PLUS 3240000) PLUS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT direction-x IS vx TIMES 1000 APPORTIONED AMONG vlength.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT direction-y IS vy TIMES 1000 APPORTIONED AMONG vlength.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT direction-z IS 1800000 APPORTIONED AMONG vlength.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT strike IS THE FINDING OF march REGARDING 0 AND 800 AND -3500 AND direction-x AND direction-y AND direction-z.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT pixel IS " ".
    SHOULD THE hit ENTERED IN strike EQUAL SUSTAINED, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT pixel IS THE FINDING OF surface-shade REGARDING (THE x ENTERED IN strike) AND (THE y ENTERED IN strike) AND (THE z ENTERED IN strike).
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS frame PLUS pixel.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS column PLUS 1.
    SHOULD column FALL SHORT OF wide, REFER TO ARTICLE 3.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS frame PLUS "\n".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS row PLUS 1.
    SHOULD row FALL SHORT OF tall, REFER TO ARTICLE 2.
    PROCLAIM frame.
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.

THE OFFICE OF field-root, CONCERNING n.
    SHOULD n FAIL TO EXCEED 0, REMAND WITH 0.
    OFF THE RECORD: Half the input plus one stays above its root for n >= 4
    OFF THE RECORD: without risking an overflowing first Newton average.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS n APPORTIONED AMONG 2 PLUS 1.
    OFF THE RECORD: Start closer to the answer while staying above it.
    OFF THE RECORD: 32768 squared is 1073741824, and 32 squared is 1024.
    SHOULD n FAIL TO EXCEED 1073741824, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS 32768.
    SHOULD n FAIL TO EXCEED 1024, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS 32.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-next IS (root-current PLUS n APPORTIONED AMONG root-current) APPORTIONED AMONG 2.
SECTION 1.
    SHOULD root-next FAIL TO FALL SHORT OF root-current, REMAND WITH root-current.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS root-next.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-next IS (root-current PLUS n APPORTIONED AMONG root-current) APPORTIONED AMONG 2.
    REFER TO SECTION 1.

THE OFFICE OF scene-distance, CONCERNING x AND y AND z.
    OFF THE RECORD: The minimum combines sphere radii 750 and 500 with the
    OFF THE RECORD: floor y = -800. Negative distances are inside a surface.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT nearest IS y PLUS 800.
    OFF THE RECORD: Neither sphere extends below the floor. Beneath it,
    OFF THE RECORD: the floor is always the nearest signed surface.
    SHOULD nearest FALL SHORT OF 0, REMAND WITH nearest.
    OFF THE RECORD: A squared bound avoids a root when the sphere cannot
    OFF THE RECORD: improve the minimum. This preserves the exact distance.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT sphere-one-squared IS x TIMES x PLUS y TIMES y PLUS z TIMES z.
    SHOULD sphere-one-squared FALL SHORT OF (nearest PLUS 750) TIMES (nearest PLUS 750), LET IT BE RECORDED THAT nearest IS (THE FINDING OF field-root REGARDING sphere-one-squared) LESS 750.
    SHOULD nearest FAIL TO EXCEED -500, REMAND WITH nearest.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT sphere-two-squared IS (x LESS 1100) TIMES (x LESS 1100) PLUS (y PLUS 300) TIMES (y PLUS 300) PLUS (z LESS 700) TIMES (z LESS 700).
    SHOULD sphere-two-squared FALL SHORT OF (nearest PLUS 500) TIMES (nearest PLUS 500), LET IT BE RECORDED THAT nearest IS (THE FINDING OF field-root REGARDING sphere-two-squared) LESS 500.
    REMAND WITH nearest.

THE OFFICE OF march, CONCERNING ox AND oy AND oz AND dx AND dy AND dz.
    OFF THE RECORD: All surfaces lie at or below y = 750. A ray above that
    OFF THE RECORD: plane and moving level or upward cannot reach the scene.
    SHOULD oy EXCEED 750 AND ALSO dy FAIL TO FALL SHORT OF 0, REMAND WITH AN EXHIBIT OF march-result WHEREIN hit IS OVERRULED AND x IS ox AND y IS oy AND z IS oz AND steps IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ray-travel IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ray-steps IS 0.
SECTION 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ray-x IS ox PLUS dx TIMES ray-travel APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ray-y IS oy PLUS dy TIMES ray-travel APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ray-z IS oz PLUS dz TIMES ray-travel APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ray-distance IS THE FINDING OF scene-distance REGARDING ray-x AND ray-y AND ray-z.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ray-steps IS ray-steps PLUS 1.
    SHOULD ray-distance FAIL TO EXCEED hit-epsilon, REMAND WITH AN EXHIBIT OF march-result WHEREIN hit IS SUSTAINED AND x IS ray-x AND y IS ray-y AND z IS ray-z AND steps IS ray-steps.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ray-travel IS ray-travel PLUS ray-distance.
    SHOULD ray-travel EXCEED far-limit OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE ray-steps EQUAL march-limit, REMAND WITH AN EXHIBIT OF march-result WHEREIN hit IS OVERRULED AND x IS ray-x AND y IS ray-y AND z IS ray-z AND steps IS ray-steps.
    REFER TO SECTION 1.

THE OFFICE OF surface-shade, CONCERNING x AND y AND z.
    OFF THE RECORD: Far from the second sphere, a floor hit has a known
    OFF THE RECORD: normal. The first sphere ends 50 units above the floor.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT normal-x IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT normal-y IS 24.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT normal-z IS 0.
    SHOULD y FAIL TO EXCEED -796 AND ALSO (x LESS 1100) TIMES (x LESS 1100) PLUS (z LESS 700) TIMES (z LESS 700) EXCEED 250000, REFER TO SECTION 1.
    OFF THE RECORD: Central differences estimate the surface normal. A
    OFF THE RECORD: 12-unit stencil spans three times the hit tolerance.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT normal-x IS (THE FINDING OF scene-distance REGARDING x PLUS 12 AND y AND z) LESS (THE FINDING OF scene-distance REGARDING x LESS 12 AND y AND z).
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT normal-y IS (THE FINDING OF scene-distance REGARDING x AND y PLUS 12 AND z) LESS (THE FINDING OF scene-distance REGARDING x AND y LESS 12 AND z).
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT normal-z IS (THE FINDING OF scene-distance REGARDING x AND y AND z PLUS 12) LESS (THE FINDING OF scene-distance REGARDING x AND y AND z LESS 12).
SECTION 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT normal-length IS THE FINDING OF field-root REGARDING normal-x TIMES normal-x PLUS normal-y TIMES normal-y PLUS normal-z TIMES normal-z.
    SHOULD normal-length EQUAL 0, REMAND WITH ".".
    OFF THE RECORD: The light points toward (-1, 1, -1). Its normalized
    OFF THE RECORD: components are approximately (-577, 577, -577).
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT diffuse IS (normal-y LESS normal-x LESS normal-z) TIMES 577 APPORTIONED AMONG normal-length.
    SHOULD diffuse FALL SHORT OF 0, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT diffuse IS 0.
    SHOULD diffuse EXCEED 1000, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT diffuse IS 1000.
    OFF THE RECORD: Offset the shadow origin by 24 units along the normal.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-x IS x PLUS normal-x TIMES 24 APPORTIONED AMONG normal-length.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-y IS y PLUS normal-y TIMES 24 APPORTIONED AMONG normal-length.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-z IS z PLUS normal-z TIMES 24 APPORTIONED AMONG normal-length.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT blocked IS THE FINDING OF shadowed REGARDING shadow-x AND shadow-y AND shadow-z.
    SHOULD blocked EQUAL SUSTAINED, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT diffuse IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shade-index IS 2 PLUS diffuse TIMES 8 APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    REMAND WITH AN EXCERPT OF ramp FROM shade-index TO shade-index.

THE OFFICE OF shadowed, CONCERNING ox AND oy AND oz.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-travel IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-steps IS 0.
SECTION 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-offset IS shadow-travel TIMES 577 APPORTIONED AMONG 1000.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-distance IS THE FINDING OF scene-distance REGARDING ox LESS shadow-offset AND oy PLUS shadow-offset AND oz LESS shadow-offset.
    SHOULD shadow-distance FAIL TO EXCEED hit-epsilon, REMAND WITH SUSTAINED.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-travel IS shadow-travel PLUS shadow-distance.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shadow-steps IS shadow-steps PLUS 1.
    SHOULD shadow-travel EXCEED far-limit OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE shadow-steps EQUAL march-limit, REMAND WITH OVERRULED.
    REFER TO SECTION 1.
